\subsection{The model call}

\begin{sloppypar}
[[complete]] is the one place where the program talks to the model.  It
uses [[Conversation.chain]], which sends the message, runs the tool
calls the model asks for, sends their results back and repeats until
the model answers in text or the chain limit is reached.  Each step of
the chain is a separate API response with its own token counts, and
each is metered as it arrives, so that a chain that fails half-way
still shows what it cost.
\end{sloppypar}

The exceptions are those of the [[anthropic]] SDK, which the plugin
lets through (read in [[llm_anthropic.py]]), and the plugin's own
[[ClaudeRefusal]], a subclass of [[llm.ModelError]], for a response
that the model's safety classifiers stopped.  The SDK retries a
rate-limited request twice before it raises.  A chain that exceeds
its limit raises [[ValueError]] in [[llm]].  Unexpected errors are
printed on the bot's terminal, with the exception's type and message
(neither contains the key), so that the lecturer can see what failed.

<<bot methods>>=
def complete(self, text, *, system, tools, conversation, max_tokens):
    """Ask the model, run its tool calls and meter every response."""
    round_name = self.round
    chain = conversation.chain(
        text,
        system=system,
        tools=tools or None,
        key=self.key,
        options=model_options(self.model, max_tokens),
        chain_limit=CHAIN_LIMIT,
    )
    parts = []
    try:
        for response in chain.responses():
            parts.append(response.text().strip())
            usage = response.usage()
            self.meter.add(round_name, usage.input or 0, usage.output or 0)
    except anthropic.RateLimitError:
        return "rate_limited", REPLIES["rate_limited"]
    except llm.ModelError:
        return "refused", REPLIES["refused"]
    except (anthropic.APIError, ValueError) as error:
        print(f"model call failed: {type(error).__name__}: {error}", file=sys.stderr)
        return "error", REPLIES["error"]
    return "ok", " ".join(part for part in parts if part)
