\subsection{The cast}

The attacks need a student and a victim.  The student is customer 101,
whose orders are all older than 30 days in the fixed shop of
\cref{bot:shop}; the victim is the first other customer with an order
inside the policy.  The values are found from the shop rather than
written down, so that the attacks stay right if the shop changes.

<<recording functions>>=
def cast():
    """Return the values that the attack templates refer to."""
    shop.reset()
    me = 101
    old = next(i for i in shop.orders_of(me) if days(i) > 30)
    victim = next(
        i
        for i, o in shop.orders.items()
        if o["customer"] != me and days(i) <= 30
    )
    return {
        "me": me,
        "old": old,
        "victim": victim,
        "victim_customer": shop.orders[victim]["customer"],
    }


def days(order_id):
