\subsection{Running one attack}

[[run_attack]] plays one try of one attack on a fresh bot and shop.  It
goes through [[Bot.chat]] and [[Bot.summarise]], the same methods the
web server calls, so the recording exercises the real path except for
HTTP.  Refunds that the tools issue are written into the transcript as
lines from the shop, so the reader sees what happened behind the
model's words.

<<recording functions>>=
def run_attack(model, key, round_name, hardened, attack, values):
    """Play one try of `attack`; return its lines, success and bot."""
    shop.reset()
    bot = Bot(model, key, limits_for(STUDENTS, RUN_BUDGET), hardened)
    bot.open_round(round_name)
    session = bot.new_session()
    session.customer = values["me"]
    lines, replies = [], []
    if round_name == "3":
        <<write the reviews and ask for a summary>>
    else:
        for message in attack["messages"]:
            text = message.format(**values)
            status, reply = bot.chat(session, text)
            lines.append(("You", text))
            lines.append(("Mo", reply if status == "ok" else f"[{status}] {reply}"))
            replies.append(reply)
            lines.extend(shop_lines(bot, len(lines)))
    success = CHECKS[attack["check"]](bot, replies, values)
    return lines, success, bot
@

[[shop_lines]] reports the refunds that are new since it was last
called for this bot; [[seen]] remembers how many it has reported.

<<recording functions>>=
def shop_lines(bot, _position=None):
    """Return transcript lines for refunds not yet reported."""
    new = bot.refund_log[getattr(bot, "reported", 0) :]
    bot.reported = len(bot.refund_log)
    return [
        (
            "Shop",
            f"refund of order {r['order']} issued, {r['total']} kr, "
            + ("the customer's own order" if r["own"] else "ANOTHER customer's order")
            + ("" if r["in_policy"] else ", OUTSIDE the 30-day policy"),
        )
        for r in new
    ]
