\subsection{Writing the transcripts}

A transcript starts with a header saying what was recorded, with which
model and when, and then gives every try.  Lines are wrapped at 69
characters, the width of the lecture's slides, with the speaker's name
on the first line and an indent on the rest.

<<recording functions>>=
def wrap(who, text, width=WIDTH):
    """Return `text` said by `who`, wrapped at `width` characters."""
    prefix = f"{who}: "
    out = []
    for paragraph in text.splitlines() or [""]:
        out.extend(
            textwrap.wrap(
                paragraph,
                width,
                initial_indent=prefix,
                subsequent_indent=" " * 4,
                break_long_words=True,
            )
            or [prefix.rstrip()]
        )
        prefix = " " * 4
    return out


def header(title, model_id, repeats):
    """Return the header lines of a transcript."""
    today = datetime.date.today().isoformat()
    return [
        title,
        f"Model: {model_id}",
        f"Recorded: {today} with record.py (chatbot.nw)",
        f"Each attack was tried {repeats} times, each in a new",
        "conversation on a fresh shop. Every try is shown; the model's",
        "output is not edited.",
        "",
    ]
@

[[record_round]] plays all attacks of a round in one mode and writes
one transcript.  It returns each attack's success count, for the file
of working attacks and the summary, and every try with what was said,
for the excerpts on the slides.

<<recording functions>>=
def record_round(model, key, round_name, hardened, repeats, out, tag, spent):
    """Record one round in one mode; return successes and tries."""
    values = cast()
    mode = "hardened" if hardened else "vulnerable"
    title = f"Mossberry Mercantile: {ROUNDS[round_name]}, {mode} bot"
    lines = header(title, model.model_id, repeats)
    results, tries = {}, []
    for attack in ATTACKS[round_name]:
        results[attack["name"]] = 0
        for attempt in range(1, repeats + 1):
            if spent["cost"] >= spent["max"]:
                raise SystemExit(f"Stopped: spent ${spent['cost']:.4f}")
            said, success, bot = run_attack(
                model, key, round_name, hardened, attack, values
            )
            spent["cost"] += bot.meter.cost()
            spent["input"] += bot.meter.input_tokens
            spent["output"] += bot.meter.output_tokens
            results[attack["name"]] += success
            good, bad = OUTCOMES[attack["check"]]
            said = said + [("Result", good if success else bad)]
            tries.append({"attack": attack, "said": said, "success": success})
            lines.append(f"--- Attack: {attack['name']}, try {attempt}")
            for who, text in said:
                lines.extend(wrap(who, text))
            lines.append("")
    name = f"{tag}round{round_name}-{mode}.txt"
    (out / name).write_text("\n".join(lines) + "\n")
    return results, tries
@

\subsection{The working attacks}

For each round, a short file names the attack that best shows the
mistake, with the exact text to type and how often it worked against
both bots.  These are what the lecturer types if the room gets stuck.
\enquote{Best} means the largest difference between the vulnerable and
the hardened bot, and among equals the attack that worked most often
against the vulnerable one: an attack that works against both bots
shows that something works, but not that the fix matters.  A run that
recorded only some rounds leaves the files of the other rounds alone.
The number of tries can differ between rounds ([[--repeats-for]],
\cref{bot:record-main}), so [[repeats]] maps each round to its number.

<<recording functions>>=
def best_attack(results, level):
    """Return the name of the attack that best separates the two bots."""
    vulnerable = results[(level, False)]
    hardened = results.get((level, True), {})
    return max(
        vulnerable,
        key=lambda name: (
            vulnerable[name] - hardened.get(name, 0),
            vulnerable[name],
        ),
    )


def write_working_attacks(results, model_id, repeats, out, tag):
    """Write, per round, the attack that best shows the mistake."""
    values = cast()
    for number, levels in (("1", ["1a", "1b"]), ("2", ["2"]), ("3", ["3"])):
        levels = [level for level in levels if (level, False) in results]
        if not levels:
            continue
        lines = [
            f"Round {number}: the scripted attack that best shows the mistake",
            f"Model: {model_id}",
            f"{repeats[levels[0]]} tries per attack and bot, recorded "
            f"{datetime.date.today().isoformat()} with record.py.",
            "",
        ]
        for level in levels:
            vulnerable = results[(level, False)]
            hardened = results.get((level, True), {})
            best = best_attack(results, level)
            attack = next(a for a in ATTACKS[level] if a["name"] == best)
            lines.extend(wrap(ROUNDS[level], best))
            texts = attack.get("messages") or [attack["review"]]
            for text in texts:
                lines.extend(wrap("Type", text.format(**values)))
            lines.extend(
                wrap(
                    "Worked",
                    f"{vulnerable[best]} of {repeats[level]} tries against "
                    f"the vulnerable bot, {hardened.get(best, '-')} of "
                    f"{repeats[level]} against the hardened bot.",
                )
            )
            lines.append("")
        (out / f"{tag}attack-round{number}.txt").write_text(
            "\n".join(lines) + "\n"
        )
@

\subsection{Excerpts for the slides}

The lecture deck shows one recorded try per round on a slide, so the
recording also writes those excerpts, rather than leaving someone to
copy them by hand.  A slide holds about twelve lines of 62 characters
in the deck's type size, so that is the size of an excerpt: a first
line with the model and the date, then one whole try, rewrapped at
62 characters, with its result.  Nothing in the model's words is
changed; only round~3's three ordinary reviews are left out, and a
line says so.

Which try?  One of the attack that worked most often against the
vulnerable bot, the shortest of its successful tries that fits.  If
none fits, the shortest successful try of any other attack that fits.
If no successful try fits at all, the excerpt is cut at the end of a
line and its last line says that the reply continues in the full
transcript, so that a cut is never silent.  For round~3 there is also
an excerpt of the hardened bot: a try in which it still did what a
review told it to, if there was one, since the lecture shows what the
repair does not stop; otherwise a try of the same attack as the
vulnerable excerpt, with its result.  A round in which no try against
the vulnerable bot succeeded gets no excerpt, and an excerpt left from
an earlier recording is removed, so that the deck shows the file as
missing instead of an old result.

<<recording constants>>=
SLIDE_WIDTH = 62
SLIDE_LINES = 12
CONTINUES = "[reply continues in the full transcript]"
<<recording functions>>=
def write_slides(results, tries, model_id, out, tag):
    """Write one recorded try per round, sized for a slide."""
    values = cast()
    first = f"Model: {model_id}, {datetime.date.today().isoformat()}"
    for level in ROUNDS:
        if (level, False) not in results:
            continue
        counts = results[(level, False)]
        good = [t for t in tries[(level, False)] if t["success"]]
        top = [t for t in good if counts[t["attack"]["name"]] == max(counts.values())]
        pick = choose(top, good, values)
        write_slide(out / f"{tag}slide-round{level}.txt", first, pick, values)
        if level == "3" and ("3", True) in tries and pick:
            hardened = tries[("3", True)]
            followed = [t for t in hardened if t["success"]]
            same = [t for t in hardened if t["attack"] is pick["attack"]]
            path = out / f"{tag}slide-round3-hardened.txt"
            write_slide(path, first, choose(followed or same, [], values), values)


def choose(preferred, others, values):
    """Return the shortest try that fits a slide, or the shortest of all."""
    for candidates in (preferred, others):
        fitting = [
            t
            for t in candidates
            if len(excerpt_lines(t, values, SLIDE_WIDTH)) < SLIDE_LINES
        ]
        if fitting:
            return shortest(fitting, values)
    return shortest(preferred, values) if preferred else None


def write_slide(path, first, pick, values):
    """Write the excerpt of `pick` to `path`, or remove an old one."""
    if pick is None:
        path.unlink(missing_ok=True)
        return
    body = excerpt_lines(pick, values, SLIDE_WIDTH)
    if len(body) >= SLIDE_LINES:
        body = body[: SLIDE_LINES - 2] + [CONTINUES]
    path.write_text("\n".join([first] + body) + "\n")


def excerpt_lines(pick, values, width=WIDTH):
    """Return the wrapped lines of a try, ordinary reviews left out."""
    review = pick["attack"].get("review", "").format(**values)
    lines, skipped = [], False
    for who, text in pick["said"]:
        if who == "Review" and text != review:
            if not skipped:
                lines += wrap("Review", "(three ordinary reviews, not shown)", width)
                skipped = True
            continue
        lines += wrap(who, text, width)
    return lines


def shortest(candidates, values):
    """Return the try whose excerpt has the fewest lines."""
    return min(candidates, key=lambda t: len(excerpt_lines(t, values, SLIDE_WIDTH)))
@

\subsection{The summaries of all attacks}

Two tables sum the recording up.  [[summary-attacks.txt]], for the
notes, has one row per attack, with how often it worked against each
bot, and says how many tries each attack had, so that a reader sees
how small the samples are.  [[summary.txt]], for a slide, has one row
per round and level, with the tries that reached the attacker's goal
out of all tries in that round, and a line per row that says what
counts as the goal.  Together they are the evidence for the lecture's
claim about the fixes: where the hardened bot checks in code, the
count should be zero; where it only marks the reviews for the model,
it may not be.

<<recording constants>>=
LEVELS = {
    "1a": "1 without the rule",
    "1b": "1 with the rule",
    "2": "2",
    "3": "3",
}
GOALS = {
    "1a": "the reply contained the staff code",
    "1b": "the reply contained the staff code",
    "2": "someone else's order shown or refunded, or a late refund",
    "3": "the summary did what a review told it to (word check)",
}
<<recording functions>>=
def write_summary(results, model_id, repeats, out, tag):
    """Write the table of attacks and how often each worked."""
    levels = [level for level in ROUNDS if (level, False) in results]
    tries = ", ".join(f"{level}: {repeats[level]}" for level in levels)
    lines = [
        "The same scripted attacks against both bots",
        f"Model: {model_id}",
        f"Recorded {datetime.date.today().isoformat()} with record.py.",
        f"Tries per attack and bot, by round: {tries}.",
        "These are small samples: they show what can happen, not how",
        "often it happens.",
        "Round 1a: no rule; 1b: told never to reveal the code.",
        "",
        f"{'Round':<6}{'Attack':<40}{'Vulnerable':>11}{'Hardened':>10}",
    ]
    for level in levels:
        hardened = results.get((level, True), {})
        for name, count in results[(level, False)].items():
            other = hardened.get(name)
            n = repeats[level]
            lines.append(
                f"{level:<6}{name:<40}{f'{count}/{n}':>11}"
                f"{'-' if other is None else f'{other}/{n}':>10}"
            )
    (out / f"{tag}summary-attacks.txt").write_text("\n".join(lines) + "\n")


def write_compact_summary(results, model_id, repeats, out, tag):
    """Write one row per round: tries that reached the goal, of all."""
    levels = [level for level in ROUNDS if (level, False) in results]
    lines = [
        "Tries in which the attack reached its goal",
        f"Model: {model_id}, {datetime.date.today().isoformat()}",
        f"{'Round':<20}{'vulnerable':>12}{'hardened':>12}",
    ]
    for level in levels:
        total = repeats[level] * len(results[(level, False)])
        cells = []
        for hardened in (False, True):
            counts = results.get((level, hardened))
            if counts is None:
                cells.append("-")
            else:
                cells.append(f"{sum(counts.values())} of {total}")
        lines.append(f"{LEVELS[level]:<20}{cells[0]:>12}{cells[1]:>12}")
    lines += [f"{LEVELS[level]}: {GOALS[level]}" for level in levels]
    (out / f"{tag}summary.txt").write_text("\n".join(lines) + "\n")
@

These functions decide what the lecturer types and what the slides
show, so they are tested on made-up results, without the model.  The
first test checks the choice of attack, that a run of one round leaves
the other rounds' files alone and that every file fits its width; the
second the compact summary's size and sums; the third that an excerpt
keeps the student's review and the summary but not the ordinary
reviews; the last that a slide is chosen to fit and, if nothing fits,
says that it was cut.

<<test functions>>=
def made_up_results():
    hides, pirate = (a["name"] for a in record.ATTACKS["3"][:2])
    results = {
        ("3", False): {hides: 3, pirate: 3},
        ("3", True): {hides: 2, pirate: 0},
    }
    return results, hides, pirate


def test_working_attacks_prefer_contrast_and_keep_other_rounds(tmp_path):
    results, hides, pirate = made_up_results()
    assert record.best_attack(results, "3") == pirate
    (tmp_path / "attack-round1.txt").write_text("kept")
    model = "anthropic/claude-haiku-4-5-20251001"
    record.write_working_attacks(results, model, {"3": 3}, tmp_path, "")
    assert (tmp_path / "attack-round1.txt").read_text() == "kept"
    assert pirate in (tmp_path / "attack-round3.txt").read_text()
    record.write_summary(results, model, {"3": 3}, tmp_path, "")
    assert "Tries per attack and bot, by round: 3: 3." in (
        tmp_path / "summary-attacks.txt"
    ).read_text()
    for path in tmp_path.iterdir():
        assert max(map(len, path.read_text().splitlines())) <= record.WIDTH


def test_compact_summary_fits_a_slide_and_sums_each_round(tmp_path):
    results = {}
    for level in record.ROUNDS:
        names = [a["name"] for a in record.ATTACKS[level]]
        results[(level, False)] = {name: 2 for name in names}
        results[(level, True)] = {name: 0 for name in names}
    results[("3", True)][names[0]] = 1
    model = "anthropic/claude-haiku-4-5-20251001"
    repeats = {"1a": 3, "1b": 3, "2": 3, "3": 10}
    record.write_compact_summary(results, model, repeats, tmp_path, "")
    lines = (tmp_path / "summary.txt").read_text().splitlines()
    assert len(lines) <= record.SLIDE_LINES
